From: Orange Pi 3 PCIe diagnostics
Subject: [PATCH] r8169: use MSI only for RTL8168F

For RTL8168F/8111F versions 35 and 36, request MSI without MSI-X or INTx
fallback so the v12 result can be compared against the vendor kernel's
working MSI path.  Leave every other MAC version's policy unchanged.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
index 293db7f..9aa8de3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
@@ -5171,7 +5171,10 @@ static int rtl_alloc_irq(struct rtl8169_private *tp)
 	case RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_07 ... RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_17:
 		flags = PCI_IRQ_LEGACY;
 		break;
+	case RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_35 ... RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_36:
+		flags = PCI_IRQ_MSI;
+		break;
 	default:
 		flags = PCI_IRQ_ALL_TYPES;
 		break;
 	}
-- 
2.50.1
